    "description": "The Cabbage Patch is one of the most accessible roadside areas in the canyon. Jack's Boulder just feet from parking is loaded with popular moderates like 'Jack's Slab' and intermediates like 'Fat Albert Gang' and 'Fungus' and the ever popular 'Double Dyno' is just up hill. The 'Dean Problem' and its harder variations on the back of Jack's are some of the most interesting shothole climbing in the canyon, and reach into the advanced range. To the west 'Tom's Problem' is a popular intermediate, and just above it the Bagins cave houses a myriad of popular advanced and elite variations. To the west the Tiger Snake has several worthy lines and the area uphill around the Monolith also has many good lines including the new 'Luke's Dyno'."
