    "latitude": "40.57994000",
    "longitude": "-111.78923000",
    "description": "An expansive boulder covered hillside north west of the canyon entrance, Outer Canyon gets year round sun, so it's a good place for Winter climbing, and gets quite hot in the summer. Some of the rock can be rather chossy, but a few gems are worth the hike including the massive Golden Egg, crystal covered Gemstone, and the Feature covered Dice Cube. There are also several excellent kid friendly boulders like The Shard, and The Birth Mark. Ever wish you could bring pooch to LCC? You're in luck! Outer Canyon is also the only boulder area in Little Cottonwood where dogs are allowed. Some boulders are on private property, but Salt Lake City is OK with bouldering as long as people stay away from the clearly marked water tanks, control startion, and service road in the Shark Tooth and Pioneer sub areas."
