    "latitude": "40.57321000",
    "longitude": "-111.74769000",
    "description": "The Hill is a steep area of densely packed boulders with a few outlying areas on the edges. It is known for elite lines like 'Triple Threat', 'Sean John', and 'Dominatrix' but is also home to loads of easier high quality problems. There are excellent tall slabs and moderate lines throughout the area starting with some good problems on the Obelisk and Stick boulders right near the road. Several popular intermediate lines can be found on Tom's Wall along with many others spread around The Hill. 'Wormography' and 'H King' are two excellent advanced problems along with the harder 'Jumper', 'Loggerhead' to the east and the very exciting 'Holy Moly' high up on the cliff band. Due to its faint trails and steep complex layout The Hill is less traveled, and still holds many projects across the grades for those willing to venture..."
